= November 2020 — After the first marches

Organisers face threats, police pressure, exhaustion and internal arguments
over tactics. Some protests enter churches. The movement's demands expand
beyond one judgment, while party leaders want a message that fits a ballot.

- @strike_defence
- @strike_programme
- @strike_condemn
- @strike_order

@strike_defence
title: Build an independent legal-defence and safety network
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Durable capacity, little immediate polling.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; feminist_trust += 10; movement_autonomy += 10; organiser_energy += 10; police_trust += 1; progressive_credibility += 3; womens_strike_followup = "Independent legal defence"; news_headline = "Legal defence keeps organisers in public life"

The network documents threats, provides lawyers and refuses party control of
cases. It will remain useful when turnout falls.

- @poland_foreign_events.us_election_2020: Follow the 3 November result

@strike_programme
title: Tie reproductive freedom to work, care and housing
subtitle: Broader coalition; risks diluting the immediate demand.
