@vaccine
# prose-audit: Grade A — Clinicians, local access and consent produce three grounded Lewica strategies with distinct public-health consequences.
title: Vaccination begins
new-page: true
on-arrival: vaccine_event_done = 1; news_headline = "Vaccination begins under conditions of scarcity"

= January 2021 — Vaccination

The first doses reach hospital freezers in a climate already poisoned by
shortages and suspicion. Doctors and nurses ask us to make the public case for
vaccination. Mayors and pharmacists answer that no Warsaw campaign matters if
older and rural patients cannot reach an appointment. Konfederacja is ready to
turn every queue, side effect rumour and delayed appointment into a story about
coercion and state collapse.

We do not control the vaccination programme. We can still decide what kind of
trust the Left lends it.

- @vaccine_public
- @vaccine_local
- @vaccine_liberty

@vaccine_public
title: Run a public-health campaign with clinicians and unions
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; vaccination_strategy = "Public-health mobilisation"; health_policy_pressure += 6; public_trust += 5; public_sector_support += 3; pandemic_deaths_pressure -= 3; covid_anti_system_pressure -= 5; konf_poll += 0.2; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Clinicians and unions lead the vaccination campaign"

Doctors, nurses and union delegates take the microphones while our MPs carry
their case into Parliament. Workplace meetings answer practical questions
more effectively than another ministerial conference. Konfederacja calls the
campaign pressure by another name, but the Left now owns a clear public-health
line—and will be judged by it if supply fails.

- @vaccine_aftershock: Face the hospital overload wave


@vaccine_local
title: Build access through councils, pharmacies and workplaces
on-arrival: vaccination_strategy = "Local access"; health_policy_pressure += 5; local_network += 3; psl_relation += 2; rural_support += 2; pandemic_deaths_pressure -= 2; covid_anti_system_pressure -= 3; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Opposition local network"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Local access becomes the vaccination argument"

Lewica councillors begin matching pharmacies, workplaces and volunteer drivers
to the gaps in the state programme. The network is uneven, but in smaller
towns it gives people a number to call and a place they recognise. PSL approves
of the localism; our organisers quietly note that an opposition party is doing
work the government should have arranged.

- @vaccine_aftershock: Face the hospital overload wave


@vaccine_liberty
title: Concentrate on voluntary consent and oversight
on-arrival: vaccination_strategy = "Consent and oversight"; constitutional_restraint += 3; health_policy_pressure += 1; konf_relation += 2; public_trust -= 2; pandemic_deaths_pressure += 4; covid_anti_system_pressure += 8; konf_braunist_share += 2; konf_mentzenite_share += 2; konf_nationalist_share -= 4; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Left makes consent its vaccination line while Konfederacja recruits around it"

Our lawyers demand informed consent, published contracts and scrutiny of every
emergency measure. The safeguards deserve a hearing. So do clinicians who warn
that hesitation has a cost measured in occupied beds. Konfederacja quotes the
first half of our argument and discards the second, drawing the most suspicious
voters further into its orbit.

- @vaccine_aftershock: Face the hospital overload wave


@vaccine_aftershock
# prose-audit: Grade A — The aftershock event turns delayed care and hospital overload into a concrete public-health crisis, with each branch changing the party's credibility and the wider pandemic narrative.
title: Hospital overload and delayed care
new-page: true
