Our amendment is short and expensive: a closure is a redundancy, and a
redundancy needs a payment, a retraining place and a date. We supply the votes
on condition that the workers on those farms are not asked to absorb a
political quarrel between two wings of the governing party.

It is the first time in this parliament that a welfare reform and a labour
guarantee arrive in the same bill, and it gives our organisers something to say
in counties where the word *Lewica* has meant nothing for a decade.

