The referral is narrow and citable: the conviction, the visa-free entry, the
public hall, the deputy who hosted him, and the sentence about the Kalashnikov
spoken by a member of the Sejm. We ask the prosecution service what it intends
to do and we ask the Marshal's office under what standard a deputy's public
events are held.

Nothing happens. The prosecution service answers to <span class="party-pis"><b>Zbigniew Ziobro</b></span>,
who is Prosecutor General as well as justice minister and does not require
anybody's countersignature to do nothing, and Braun spends a fortnight being
persecuted on camera, which is the role he came for.

