= November 2020 — Blocking the money to keep the courts

Poland and Hungary announce they will veto the European Union's seven-year
budget and the pandemic recovery fund, because both come attached to a mechanism linking
payments to the rule of law. **Zbigniew Ziobro** and Solidarna Polska treat the
veto as the whole point of being in government. Gowin's people and much of the
finance ministry regard it as setting fire to a hundred and seventy billion
euro to protect a disciplinary chamber.

Prime Minister **Mateusz Morawiecki** has to hold a coalition that agrees on
nothing here, against a Union that has already worked out it can build the fund
without the two vetoing members if it has to.

[? if united_right_cohesion <= 45: The governing camp is already visibly
fraying, which makes its internal price for this veto higher than its external
one.?]
[? if nik_referral_channel = 1: Our audit-chamber channel means we can put a
number on what a delayed cohesion payment does to a specific voivodeship rather
than arguing about it.?]

- @euveto_conditionality
- @euveto_hospitals
- @euveto_sovereignty
- @euveto_gowin

