Witek takes the chair. Our deputies vote against and say nothing further,
because a caucus of forty-nine has to choose what it spends November on and we
have chosen the presidential campaign.

Nobody remembers this in November. The chamber's rules are now entirely the
majority's, and the next four years will test how much that was worth saving a
week for.

