The suspensions stand. The message is received exactly as intended: the party
being built this summer will have one discipline, and it belongs to the people
running the merger.

Six deputies spend the unification congress as spectators with grievances and
telephones. Every splinter conversation that happens in this parliament — and
several happen — starts from the list of people who were suspended in May.

