Three people none of the currents chose, a written procedure, and a decision
that binds the leadership as much as the deputies. It reinstates four, upholds
two with a reprimand, and satisfies nobody, which is the standard evidence that
an arbitration is real.

The body outlives the case. It is the reason the next internal crisis — and
there is always a next one — is argued in front of somebody rather than
announced by press release.

